  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "mW5AXYZkn7D57jQlVRcWm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 112.13815129565933,
      "y": -108.46709180153093,
      "width": 1535.720947265625,
      "height": 1138.0824123092166,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2109469817,
      "version": 1971,
      "versionNonce": 682255609,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779073507432,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements\nSubmit (Source, Destination) -> Get Ride Types and fares -> Submit Ride Type Selection ->Searches Best Ride (GeoHashing) -> Get Rider Details after confirmation\n1) Users should be able to retrieve ride types and ride fair\n2) Users should be able to Book Rides\n3) Users and Drivers should be able to Cancel Ride, drivers should be able to accept rides.\n4) Call, message \n5) Rating \n\nNon-Functional Requirements\nCAP (Availability and Partition Tolerance)\n1) Highly Available\n2) Scalable, able to handle peak traffic bookings request (high throughput)\n3) low latency matching\n4) Rider:Driver (1:1) matching\n\nAPI Specifications\n\n1) GET -> v1/rideTypeAndFare \n    { src,\n     dest }\n\n2) POST -> v1/bookRide\n    {\n        userId,\n        rideTypeIdAndFare\n    }\n\n3) POST -> v1/cancelRide\n    {\n        rideId\n    }\n\n4) Post -> v1/review\n    {\n        driverId\n        review\n    }\n\nDATABASE CHOICE :\n    Do we need complex/flexible query functionalities -> No -> NoSQL\n                                   (SQL supports complex queries)\n    Is their relational nature in the data to be stored -> No -> NoSQL\n    Do we need ACID properties or transactional -> No -> NoSQL\n    Availability -> High availability High performance - > NoSQL (DynamoDB)\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 18.96804020515361,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements\nSubmit (Source, Destination) -> Get Ride Types and fares -> Submit Ride Type Selection ->Searches Best Ride (GeoHashing) -> Get Rider Details after confirmation\n1) Users should be able to retrieve ride types and ride fair\n2) Users should be able to Book Rides\n3) Users and Drivers should be able to Cancel Ride, drivers should be able to accept rides.\n4) Call, message \n5) Rating \n\nNon-Functional Requirements\nCAP (Availability and Partition Tolerance)\n1) Highly Available\n2) Scalable, able to handle peak traffic bookings request (high throughput)\n3) low latency matching\n4) Rider:Driver (1:1) matching\n\nAPI Specifications\n\n1) GET -> v1/rideTypeAndFare \n    { src,\n     dest }\n\n2) POST -> v1/bookRide\n    {\n        userId,\n        rideTypeIdAndFare\n    }\n\n3) POST -> v1/cancelRide\n    {\n        rideId\n    }\n\n4) Post -> v1/review\n    {\n        driverId\n        review\n    }\n\nDATABASE CHOICE :\n    Do we need complex/flexible query functionalities -> No -> NoSQL\n                                   (SQL supports complex queries)\n    Is their relational nature in the data to be stored -> No -> NoSQL\n    Do we need ACID properties or transactional -> No -> NoSQL\n    Availability -> High availability High performance - > NoSQL (DynamoDB)\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
